# List Row Actions — Three-Dot Menu Pattern

When a list row has **more than one action**, the actions MUST be grouped inside a three-dot menu (`TemplateRowMenu` or equivalent). Never place multiple visible action buttons directly in a row.

## ✅ CORRECT — Multiple actions go in a menu

```jsx
// Reuse TemplateRowMenu from TrainingTemplates.jsx pattern
<TemplateRowMenu
  ariaLabel={`Ações do item ${item.name}`}
  onEdit={() => handleEdit(item)}
  onDelete={() => handleDelete(item.id)}
  deleteLabel="Remover"  // optional, defaults to "Excluir"
/>
```

## ❌ WRONG — Multiple buttons directly in the row

```jsx
<button onClick={() => handleEdit(item)}>Editar</button>
<button onClick={() => handleDelete(item.id)}>Excluir</button>
```

## ✅ CORRECT — Single action can be a direct button

```jsx
// Only one action: direct button is fine
<button className="btn-delete-sm" onClick={() => handleRemove(id)}>
  Remover
</button>
```

## Implementation Details

The `TemplateRowMenu` component (defined in `src/pages/trainer/TrainingTemplates.jsx`) accepts:
- `ariaLabel` (required) — describes the item, e.g. `Ações do treino ${name}`
- `onDelete` (required) — handler for the destructive action
- `onEdit` (optional) — handler for the edit action; omit to hide the edit item
- `deleteLabel` (optional) — label for destructive action, defaults to `"Excluir"`

The trigger button uses `MoreVertical` from `lucide-react` and implements click-outside detection to close the dropdown.

## When Applying This Rule

- **New list/table rows with multiple actions:** always use the menu pattern
- **Edit + Delete/Remove:** the most common case — use `onEdit` + `onDelete`
- **aria-label for trigger:** must identify the item, e.g. `Ações do exercício Supino Reto`
- **Destructive items:** always use `row-menu-item--danger` CSS class
